            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mcho56"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use a very similar recipe and LOVE it! The main difference is I use red onions and try like heck to let it sit overnight..wonderful!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "EscoJamie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this several times now, and it's a party in your mouth. Excellent recipe as is. I add diced jalapeno or serrano peppers since we like some heat. I've used fresh or dried cilantro depending on what was on hand. Both are good, but fresh cilantro outclasses the dried stuff for sure. Also, very important to remove the seeds and juicy middle from the tomatoes and let them dry in the colander while preparing other ingredients for a minimum of 30 minutes. Love it as dip with chips and on fish tacos too!",
            "datePublished": "2023-09-27T03:23:54.056Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "YOPI1960"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe as a base. I changed a few things. I used splenda instead of sugar. I am not a hugh cilantro fan but I know it did need some so I used a tsp of dried cilantro. I chopped up a red and yellow pepper. This added great flavor as well as color. For some added heat I chopped 1/2 of a jalapeno pepped without the seeds. I added 1/4 cup of Ball Fiesta Salsa Mix and cooked the mixture for 2 minutes. I canned my salsa for gifts. YUMMY!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-04T12:05:34.770Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aaron Galvan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This stuff is really great. ...but I changed it a bit I added a half of a Serrano pepper and put it all in a blender",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-06T11:38:39.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jody"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the first time I've made fresh salsa, and I think I prefer cooked. I threw it in a saucepan and cooked it down for about 15 minutes and liked it a lot better. I too added a green pepper and a jalapeno for a bit of heat. Also added two more teaspoons of sugar because I prefer tomatoey stuff on the sweet side. I will definitely keep this recipe but will make the same changes. Now I can be one of the people that drive everybody crazy!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-06T10:26:55.977Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rnicholson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very yummy, I actually made the mix, cooked it in a skilled for a few minutes, just until the onions got a bit translucent. I then cooked some chicken breast on the skillet with some lime juice, salt, and pepper. Once the chicken was done I sliced it thin and placed it in a tortilla. I added some cooked rice in the middle, put the mango on top and made it into a wrap. Grilled it off a bit to get a nice crunch on the outside. And wow was that ever yummy!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-20T11:22:07.417Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vikki"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful taste, no sugar is needed if your mangoes are ripe. I canned the extras, hopefully it tastes just as good as fresh made.",
            "datePublished": "2022-06-20T15:36:12.935Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andrea O."
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent!! Im a picky eater but wanted something to freshen up the same old, same old dinner. I made some slight changes. I switched lime juice to lemon 'cause I have a tree, and added a apple instead of the 1/2 of mango. The mago was too hard to cut to just use half of the second one. Instead of garlic and onion I used shalots. My husband is not a huge fan of fresh garlic. And sometimes onion can be too strong. I also added mint. I brought it to 50 year anniversary party, and everyone loved it! I will be making this again!",
            "datePublished": "2011-10-17T10:30:42.883Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lindsey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a really refreshing salsa. Even my husband liked it which was a nice surprise since he doesn't like raw onions or tomatoes. I didn't use vinegar because I didn't have any off hand but I added mint leaves and chilli powder to give it a little kick with the sweetness which was amazing! And instead of using Roma tomatoes I used yellow sunburst tomatoes. All in all very delicious",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-17T11:49:49.443Z"
          },
          {
